{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle","id":1462448,"title":"Can anyone fill me in about the Metaplot happenings around Seattle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T11:11:59-07:00","id":1462448,"title":"Can anyone fill me in about the Metaplot happenings around Seattle?","content":"So I have been considering running a Mage game, and have been brainstorming for ideas. I thought I would set it in Seattle, after the Avatar Storm. The players would be a group of Tradition mages who are in Seattle helping to build or rebuild a chantry in what was a Technocratic stronghold, and now with the coals of the Ascension War cooled (in theory,) coexisting in a tentative peace.<br /> <br /> Mostly I just think Seattle is a neat city and I would like to visit sometime, I don't actually know a ton about the city so if anyone has any insights, let me know.<br /> <br /> But I was also wondering what you guys thought might be going on metaplot-wise in Seattle. Unfortunately I am not the most knowledgeable about the Technocracy, so your insight would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> -The Void Engineers have a voidship in Seattle. This seems like it should be a big deal... I am guessing it is a big craft used to traverse the Umbra, and has probably been stuck on this side of the Umbra since the Avatar Storm. Anything I should know about voidships? <br /> <br /> -The Wiki isn't very clear on this, but the Syndicate's Special Projects Division (which is a wyrm-corrupted branch of the Syndicate) used to have a &quot;Liason&quot; to Pentex in Seattle. Would this be one person, a few people, or an entire chantry?<br /> <br /> -Also &quot;it&quot; was attacked and &quot;everyone&quot; vanished. I am not sure who &quot;it&quot; was, who attacked it and who vanished. The page on the SPD suggests that it was the Special Projects division that vanished (the entire methodology vanished?) but not who attacked it, if anyone. The page on the SPD seems to suggest it had to do with the Avatar Storm. Maybe they were all in some chantry in the Umbra when the Avatar Storm hit and got destroyed?<br /> <br /> -And why is Pentex paying dividends to the Syndicate for... nothing? I presume this is a placating measure to keep the Syndicate from investigating Pentex for losing an entire division, but this sounds a bit like hush money or blackmail or something of that kind... The Syndicate is... pretty slimy as far as technocratic conventions go, but to look the other way when an entire division goes &quot;poof?&quot; It seems like someone in the Syndicate is taking bribes to keep others from looking into the disappearance. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T13:00:29-07:00","id":1462467,"title":"","content":"It's not just a voidship, but a voidship factory. A facility like that is probably harder to operate with the more limited resources of the post-Avatar Storm period. But yeah, voidships are useful and powerful.<br /> <br /> Also, voidships are not just for traveling the Umbra, but are more like Star Trek vessels that also happen to travel in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> The wiki is not very clear on what happened to the SPD because the books were always intentionally vague about it. Pentex continuing to send big cheques is very much a carrot to add to the heads-in-boxes they sent back when the Syndicate tried investigating seriously. The Syndicate keeping on the hush is more than just them being greedy or corrupt though. They're afraid that the truth of their compromised relationship with a mega-corporation ruled by Nephandi-like Reality Deviants coming out to the rest of the Union could result in their Convention being torn apart, or the entire Technocracy descending into civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T00:55:40-07:00","id":1462777,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response. <br /> <br /> In my mind I imagined the players being contacted by a Syndicate mage (shrouded by as much identity-concealing magick as he could muster) who wants to get to the truth of the matter, but can't go through official channels, and offers them an exchange in information if they will look into the disappearance of SPD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T04:47:29-07:00","id":1462789,"title":"","content":"If you're interested; there's a lot of Wraith lore on Seattle. Its Necropolis gets a detailed write-up in the Wr20 &quot;Book of Oblivion&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T11:09:12-07:00","id":1462815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle#post1462448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I would set it in Seattle, after the Avatar Storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean:<br /> <br /> A) immediately after the Avatar Storm hits, as in it's 1999/2000?<br /> B) It's 2021 and the storm has had time to subside?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T12:27:49-07:00","id":1462824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle?p=1462815#post1462815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean:<br /> <br /> A) immediately after the Avatar Storm hits, as in it's 1999/2000?<br /> B) It's 2021 and the storm has had time to subside?</div> </div> </div> </div>B. I am picturing a situation where the storm has subsided and left the old chantries empty and in disrepair, and the Traditions and Technocracy are going back to recover what was lost... and perhaps digging up some ancient history that was better left undisturbed...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T12:29:04-07:00","id":1462825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle?p=1462789#post1462789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're interested; there's a lot of Wraith lore on Seattle. Its Necropolis gets a detailed write-up in the Wr20 &quot;Book of Oblivion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will have to check that out then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T13:52:46-07:00","id":1462835,"title":"","content":"I was doing some reading in the W20 Book of the Wyrm, and it seems to have some implications about the fate of the SPD. If I interpreted the handful of mentions that came up correctly, regarding the two Syndicate Mages contending for seats on the Board of Directors, it seems like the split was at least somewhat canon in W20, with SPD effectively being absorbed back into Pentex. The Syndicate seems wary of Pentex, but it seems like they either think they are getting the situation under control, or they are still unwilling to risk a public fallout from starting a real conflict.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ian_Robertson\" target=\"_blank\">Ian Robertson | White Wolf Wiki | Fandom</a> seems to be trying to infiltrate Pentex to bring it down, given discussion of his decision to join the Board being made in consultation with his &quot;backers&quot; (including &quot;Garou monkeywrenchers&quot;).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dr._Bentley_Chism\" target=\"_blank\">Dr. Bentley Chism | White Wolf Wiki | Fandom</a> meanwhile seems like a former SPD member who is now rejoining the Syndicate after his failed attempt at joining the Board, with the purpose of spreading Wyrm corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T21:58:28-07:00","id":1462871,"title":"","content":"<b>Hidden Lore</b> has a chapter on Seattle, with some setting notes, a chantry, NPCs, story ideas. You could give that a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T19:05:52-07:00","id":1462953,"title":"","content":"Okay, so this isn't exactly metaplot information, but it might be a good source of setting and character ideas. At 12:25, it gets into details of a political conflict over how to handle homelessness, addiction and crime. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T18:10:18-07:00","id":1463037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle?p=1462953#post1462953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so this isn't exactly metaplot information, but it might be a good source of setting and character ideas. At 12:25, it gets into details of a political conflict over how to handle homelessness, addiction and crime.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpAi70WWBlw</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I watched that this morning and it was heartbreaking. It's no wonder Brucato came up with a cabal of homeless mages for the quickstart and set it in Seattle. I think one of the themes may have to include some variation of &quot;magick can't solve everything&quot; because if it could...<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder how much responsibility I should put on supernatural groups like the Technocracy/Syndicate or Pentex for issues like this. The idea that &quot;if we could just get rid of &quot;x&quot; it would all be fine, is a very simplistic answer for an extremely complicated problem.<br /> <br /> I may not agree 100% with the documentary, but it certainly was eye-opening, thanks for sharing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T19:36:30-07:00","id":1463045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle?p=1463037#post1463037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched that this morning and it was heartbreaking. It's no wonder Brucato came up with a cabal of homeless mages for the quickstart and set it in Seattle. I think one of the themes may have to include some variation of &quot;magick can't solve everything&quot; because if it could...<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder how much responsibility I should put on supernatural groups like the Technocracy/Syndicate or Pentex for issues like this. The idea that &quot;if we could just get rid of &quot;x&quot; it would all be fine, is a very simplistic answer for an extremely complicated problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can give a clear example of why homelessness is difficult to prevent. Let's say a city wants to improve its economy and is looking at ways to do so and they want to prevent homelessness. One strategy could be to try to attract computing, engineering and biotechnology firms who will create high paying jobs. The tech workers will spend their disposable income in the local economy, creating more jobs and tax revenue. So, nobody should be homeless in this imagined future. What ends up happening is that the well paid tech workers have more money to spend on buying or renting apartments and houses, driving prices upward and pushing previous occupants, whose paychecks haven't increased, onto the street. On the other hand, if a city completely fails to attract firms that will pay these big salaries, a local recession can occur that ends up producing homelessness.<br /> <br /> In my own story, the players have the benefit of the Traditions being in control of the state government. The Technocracy know from experience what social problems you take on as moral liabilities when you try to rule. They apply this knowledge to their strategy against the Traditions. They are cold, ruthless and perfectly willing to spread misery in the sleeper population to undermine ruling Reality Deviants, believing that they can do no good with political power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462448-can-anyone-fill-me-in-about-the-metaplot-happenings-around-seattle?p=1463037#post1463037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may not agree 100% with the documentary, but it certainly was eye-opening, thanks for sharing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}